From: Hamza <155834495+lonadonia@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 21:15:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/12] marianos-azure-headless 1.10.0rc6: validate-export
 reads each stored source once with bounded memory and checks every record's
 capture and values (OR-20)

The run's sources are read, hashed against the hash the run recorded and released one at a time; the source
index keeps each distinct price statement once (SourceIndex), so memory follows a run's distinct prices, not
its pages. The supporting log is decoded one record at a time for each record's capture. Every exported
record's capture is checked: present, its bytes' SHA-256 as the log states, readable; a missing, corrupted or
unreadable capture is named and rejects the export (exit 6). Each mismatch is listed with the record's values,
the source's values and the source. The report gives the time taken, the sources read, the price statements
read and the process's peak memory.
